-band bounds. The draggable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"card responds to touch input via Origami’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"origami.Drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" patch, which wires its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"output ","type":"text"},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to the layer’s transform. When released near the center, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"card snaps back to its resting position.","type":"text"}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/scrollPosition(id:anchor:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/scrollposition(id:anchor:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView\/scrollPosition(id:anchor:)","role":"symbol","title":"scrollPosition(id:anchor:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"scrollPosition","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI7BindingV","text":"Binding","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<(","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")?>, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"anchor","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI9UnitPointV","text":"UnitPoint","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI4ViewP","text":"View","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"url":"\/documentation\/swami","title":"Swami","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","type":"topic"}}}